WinUAE-oracle Agnus/copper audit 2026-08-07
--------------------------------------------
Requested comparison of the Agnus/copper implementations against WinUAE
(custom.cpp, the 2022+ cycle-exact RGA-pipeline copper).  New testbench
tb_agnus_copper.v pins the behaviour (wired into run_tests.sh): it models
the CCK-phased beam, the odd-slot grant and the register-bus loopback.
Note the custom bus holds register writes for a FULL CCK -- a one-tick
write races the COPJMP strobe against its own clk_ena clear.

Audited CLEAN against the oracle:
  - WAIT comparison: Minimig's substitute-unmasked-bits-then-GE trick is
    equivalent to WinUAE's mask-both-sides two-stage compare (vertical
    greater wins; equal vertical compares HP8..HP1 at 2-CCK resolution);
    V7 always compared; BFD gates both WAIT and SKIP.
  - SKIP taken before a non-MOVE: the WAIT/SKIP executes normally
    (WinUAE clears skiplatch without effect) -- Minimig's 2005 "skip only
    skips MOVE" fix matches the oracle.
  - CDANG classes ($080 / $040 OCS / all ECS) match
    test_copper_dangerous exactly.
  - Wake-up consumes a free DMA slot without transferring; the
    dummy-cycle count after IR2 matches WinUAE's irload pipeline
    (4-cycle WAIT/SKIP shape).
  - Strobe/reset takes a pointer-reload DMA cycle then fetches, the
    documented 2-cycle COPJMP delay.
  - Beamcounter: VPOSR Agnus-ID composition is exactly right for
    OCS/ECS/AGA in PAL and NTSC (0x00/0x10/0x20/0x30/0x23/0x33), LOL at
    bit 7; VERTB at line 0 (line 1 with the A1000 quirk); VHPOSW/VPOSW
    write paths present; LOF toggles only under LACE.

Fixed (negative-control proven in tb_agnus_copper):
  - An illegal MOVE (CDANG-protected register) now fetches its SECOND
    instruction word into COPINS before halting, using one more DMA
    cycle, as real hardware does: WinUAE clears validmove at the IR1
    stage but the IR2 cycle is already allocated and completes; only the
    register write is suppressed.  The old code halted in FETCH2 without
    fetching, leaving a visible free slot and stale COPINS.  A new
    HALTED state holds the copper until a strobe or SOF.

Documented deviations (unchanged -- all marginal-cycle or pathological,
and the copper feeds a hardware-proven display pipeline):
  - SKIP latches its comparison ~2 CCKs earlier than WinUAE (which
    samples at the next-IR1-fetch cycle); only marginal beam-crossing
    SKIPs differ.
  - COPJMP written while a fetch is in flight: WinUAE models a strobe
    pipeline that can merge with the in-flight cycle (startstrobe
    shift); Minimig aborts to RESET at the next CCK.
  - The VHPOSW even-to-even transition copper bug (spurious DMA from
    address 0) is not modeled.
  - Blitter uses slots 1+2 instead of 1+3 (documented Minimig design
    choice for DMA contention).
  - NTSC alternating 227/228-CCK long/short lines are not implemented
    (fixed 227); LOL reads back toggling but line length is constant.
  - Sub-CCK ordering inside agnus_copper uses blocking assignments
    across always blocks (copjmp/strobe) -- functional in the shipped
    integration, but simulation-order sensitive; the TB drives writes
    with full-CCK hold like the real bus.
Systemic FPU fixes from hardware cputest screenshots (2026-08-07)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Thirteen 68040_intfpu/basicfpu failures (FDNEG.D, FDMOVE.S/P, FDIV.B/W/
D/P/X, FDDIV.B/L/S/W/X/P, FDADD.X, FABS.P) reduced to two root causes,
both pinned against the compiled WinUAE softfloat (scratchpad
fporacle/fpprobe oracles run on the exact screenshot operands):

  1. PSEUDO-DENORMALS ARE LEGAL OPERANDS.  floatx80_is_denormal
     requires the integer bit CLEAR, so an exponent-field-0 operand
     with the integer bit SET computes directly with the RAW exponent
     (value 1.m x 2^-16382-ish by encoding, raw 0 in the working
     math).  unsupported_x in ap040_fpu.v narrowed to true denormals
     (e=0, int clear, frac!=0) and true unnormals (0<e<7FFF, int
     clear, m!=0); unnormal ZEROS (m=0, any e) behave as zeros.
     Consequences pinned by the oracle: extended-precision tininess
     starts at er < 0 (not er < 1) -- er == 0 packs exponent field 0
     with the significand UNSHIFTED and NO flags; er < 0 shifts by -er
     with UNFL (INEX2 only for lost bits).  emin for extended and the
     FSGL class is now 0 in F_ROUND; F_UNFL packs exponent 0.  The
     old (1 - er) shift was validated against qemu only, and t_fpu
     93-98 carried its wrong expectations ($00100000 shift-11 and
     $40000000 halving results); both re-pinned to the softfloat
     oracle ($00200000, $80000000).  Note the 68881-fpga reference
     implements 1-exp shift with normalize-before-arithmetic: that is
     correct FOR A 68881 -- the 040 raw-exponent model is different
     architecture, not a bug in either.
  2. EVERY vector-55 fault stacks FORMAT $3.  Register and immediate
     sources have no address and stack EA = 0 (cputest frames end
     30,dc,00,00,00,00); the old format-$0 branch in go_fp_unsupp came
     from the UM 9.6.2 "pre-instruction" prose.  WinUAE get_fp_value
     inits ad = 0 and immediate operands never assign it.

Tests: h_fpunsup accepts only $30DC frames now; t_fpu 208-240 add the
screenshot vectors (FDIV.B by -1 sign-flip preserving the 0000
encoding, FDDIV.W pseudo/0 -> clean +inf + DZ, -0/pseudo -> -0 N+Z,
FDADD.X pseudo addend -> double-rounded with INEX only, unnormal-zero
addend, er==0/er<0 packing, EA=0 frames for register and immediate
sources) and 241-244 cover memory-indirect FP operands (base-suppress
indirection, odd-address word operand, outer displacement) -- the
FDIV.W ([0]) screenshot did not reproduce in sim with a correct EA
decode, so it likely shared root cause 1; hardware retest will tell.
Negative controls: reverting unsupported_x fails 210, reverting emin
fails 94, reverting the frame format fails via the handler's hfail
(id 98) at the first no-EA fault.

Retained IRQ and FPU resume fixes (2026-08-11)
------------------------------------------------
The full WinUAE IRQ and ODD_IRQ corpus exposed an instruction-boundary detail
which a combinational `IPL > SR.I` test cannot model.  Once a level 1--6
request has reached IPEND while unmasked, AP040 now retains the highest level
until exception entry acknowledges it.  An instruction which raises the SR
mask in the meantime therefore cannot erase an already-pending interrupt.
Level 7 remains a separate edge latch.  Interrupt and trace entry also pass
through `S_POST_EXC`, so same-edge BSR/JSR/DBcc and ordinary register
writeback is visible before the exception snapshot.  Verilator passes all
100 IRQ/ODD_IRQ slices, including MOVE-to-SR, AND/OR/EOR-to-SR, STOP,
control-flow and odd-vector cases.

Vector-55 register-store faults now distinguish two PCs.  A statically
unsupported packed store still reports the last consumed extension word,
whereas a datatype fault discovered by the FPU while converting an otherwise
valid store stacks the following PC.  Resuming the latter at `pc-2` had made
RTE execute the EA extension as an opcode.  The complete directed AP040 suite
and both BasicFPU FMOVE.X slices pass with the split behavior.

The 2026-08-12 full 1,911-slice Verilator sweep passes 1,875 slices with no
timeouts or harness errors.  Every non-BasicFPU/PackedFPU group is perfect,
including AE 32/32, Basic 494/494, Default 821/821, FFEXT 60/60, IRQ 92/92,
ODD_EXC/IRQ/STK 45/45, and intFPU 17/17.  BasicFPU passes 288/320 and
PackedFPU passes 24/28.  All 36 first failures decode as FPU memory-EA
instructions: 32 memory-to-FPU operations (opclass 010) and four
FPU-to-memory operations (opclass 011).  No failing slice first diverges in a
register-source arithmetic operation.  The replay log now prints the six
instruction bytes and the EA captured at FPU dispatch, and `summary.json`
records that context plus the decoded opclass and memory-EA classification.

Representative failures were reconstructed from the serialized input.  In
BasicFPU FADD.X/0001 test 182, the indirect pointer at address zero selects
$0000BFFF and all twelve serialized operand bytes there are zero, while the
oracle expects a one-bit tiny addend and INEX/UNFL status.  In FNEG.X/0003
test 203, AP040 returns the serialized low mantissa `$2FD2B162`, while the
oracle expects `$2FD20000`, a value left by an unrecorded prior generator
write.  These are instances of the v20 omitted-memory-transition defect
described in `diff/README`, not evidence for an RTL unary-rounding or
underflow change.  The failures remain visible; the harness does not xfail or
mask them.

Instruction branch-refill buffer (2026-09-02)
----------------------------------------------
A one-sector instruction refill buffer now keeps completed fetch words across
ordinary control-flow redirects and seeds the prefetch queue when all four
words beginning at the new PC are present.  The complete-window requirement
keeps partial prefixes off the redirect path.  Exceptions and all other
architectural prefetch flushes invalidate the sector; a branch redirect alone
does not.

The complete directed suite passes, including reset/double-fault, walker CDC,
16-bit bus gaps and timeouts, cache/snoop, integer, exception, MMU, cache, and
FPU tests.  Wombat's first 100 SingleStepTests CPU rows compare 1,696
architectural field groups with zero real differences.  `bench_loop` improves
from 326,674 to 289,956 clocks (11.24 percent), while the phase-0 result is
289,178 clocks.  A timing-clean Cyclone V integration at placement seed 24
also booted Mac OS 7.5.5 and completed every Speedometer 3.23 PR category.
